1. Scope and unofficial status

This license applies to the Pixelheart source code, executables, documentation,
and project-owned template material made available under these terms (the
"Software"), to the extent owned by the Pixelheart copyright holder (the "Licensor").
Separately licensed third-party components and user-provided content are
excluded.

Pixelheart is a free, unofficial community tool for Stardew Valley, a game
developed by ConcernedApe (Eric Barone). The Licensor is a devoted fan, not a
representative of ConcernedApe. Pixelheart is not affiliated with, sponsored by,
or endorsed by ConcernedApe or ConcernedApe LLC. Stardew Valley, its original
content, and its trademarks remain the property of their respective rights
holders. This license grants no rights in those third-party works or marks.

2. Personal use and private modifications

Subject to these terms, you may download, install, run, and inspect the Software
for personal, noncommercial Stardew Valley modding, make working and backup
copies for your own use, and modify a local copy solely for that use. Retain
existing copyright and license notices. The gameplay-video and livestream
exception in section 5 expressly applies despite the noncommercial condition.

3. Redistribution, reuse, and prohibited commercial exploitation

Except as permitted in sections 4 through 7 or by applicable law, prior written
permission from the Licensor is required to redistribute or rehost the Software,
publish a modified version or derivative tool, or incorporate copyright-protected
parts of it into another project. These permissions are not granted merely by
crediting the author. You may freely share the official project or download link.

Commercial exploitation of the Software is prohibited under this license.
You may not sell it, charge for access to it, paywall its source code or binaries,
license it for a fee, incorporate its code in a monetized product, or run a paid
or advertising-supported service based on it. You may not use Pixelheart to
provide paid NPC-generation services or earn Donation Points from its code or
project-owned material. Permission for noncommercial redistribution or reuse
does not waive these commercial restrictions.

This license does not permit converting Pixelheart or its project-owned
templates or assets for use in other games. It does not restrict using your
independently owned artwork or characters elsewhere without Pixelheart material.

Permission requests for noncommercial redistribution or reuse should be directed
to the Licensor through the official Pixelheart repository.

4. Free NPC packs and user content

The Licensor claims no ownership of uploaded artwork, authored dialogue,
character data, or other original user content merely because Pixelheart is
used. You may create, edit, and freely publish or share NPC packs for Stardew
Valley without separate permission from the Licensor. Credit to Pixelheart for
creating an NPC pack is appreciated but optional; third-party credit requirements
still apply.

For Pixelheart-owned template material intentionally included in normal NPC
exports, including JSON structures, starter dialogue, and pack documentation,
you may use, copy, modify, and distribute that material as part of free Stardew
Valley NPC packs and modified versions of those packs. Recipients receive the
same permission subject to these terms. Retain any supplied output-permission
notice with the pack.

You may not sell, paywall, require payment or a subscription for access to, or
earn Donation Points from packs containing this Pixelheart-owned material.
These restrictions cover the tool and its material, not the independent rights
you hold in original artwork or dialogue used outside Pixelheart. The output
permission does not authorize distributing the editor, its source code, its
executable, or a separate template library.

5. Gameplay-video and livestream exception

You may show NPC packs created with Pixelheart in Stardew Valley gameplay
videos, recordings, and livestreams, including monetized content. Advertising
revenue, channel subscriptions, viewer tips, and sponsorship of that gameplay
content are permitted under this exception. No separate Pixelheart permission
is required.

This exception permits the gameplay content and use of Pixelheart to prepare
NPCs for it. It does not permit selling or paywalling the tool, code, downloads,
or Pixelheart-owned template material, and it does not grant Donation Points
permission for mod files. You must still have the necessary rights in uploaded
artwork, music, other mods, and any other third-party material.

ConcernedApe's own gameplay-monetization policy is available at:
https://www.stardewvalley.net/stardew-monetization-policy-for-twitch-streamers-youtubers-etc/

